      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Current Cryptographic & Structural Limits Driving the Roadmap",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Current Cryptographic & Structural Limits Driving the Roadmap",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "cons_sbody_0197",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1248,
      "y": 2526,
      "width": 976,
      "height": 168,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#212529",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "cons_grp_0160"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "d0198",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 425881510,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1786149789,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794900000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\u2022 Quantum vulnerability: BLS12-381 pairings (validator keys + Sync Committee + RANDAO) are broken by Shor's algorithm.\n\u2022 Finality latency: Waiting 2 epochs of 1/32-committee rounds (~12.8\u201316 min) bottlenecks bridges & L2 settlement.\n\u2022 Proposer predictability: EIP-7917 lookahead improves preconf UX today, but exposes proposers to targeted DoS.\n\u2022 Light-client trust: Sync Committees cover only 512 randomly rotated validators rather than proving the full CL STF.",
      "fontSize": 13.5,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\u2022 Quantum vulnerability: BLS12-381 pairings (validator keys + Sync Committee + RANDAO) are broken by Shor's algorithm.\n\u2022 Finality latency: Waiting 2 epochs of 1/32-committee rounds (~12.8\u201316 min) bottlenecks bridges & L2 settlement.\n\u2022 Proposer predictability: EIP-7917 lookahead improves preconf UX today, but exposes proposers to targeted DoS.\n\u2022 Light-client trust: Sync Committees cover only 512 randomly rotated validators rather than proving the full CL STF.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.32
    },
